 "clusters_recorded": {
  "item3a_abell520": "P3 = X-ray peak without bright galaxies (\"dark core\"). Mahdavi+07 (CFHT) and Jee+12 (WFPC2) and Jee+14 (ACS) find P3 mass ~3.4-4.4e13 Msun (r<150 kpc) with M/L 326-966 (B) / 266-813 (R); Clowe+12 (ACS+Magellan) find P3 = 2.26+-0.75e13 with M/L (z band, gas-subtracted) 114+-54, consistent with other peaks -> no dark core. Jee+14 attribute part of difference to CTI correction.",
  "item3b_MACSJ0025": "Two near-equal subclusters: M(<300 kpc, projected) = 2.5(+1.0/-1.7)e14 (SE) and 2.6(+0.5/-1.4)e14 Msun (NW); gas peak between them; total-mass peaks offset from gas peak (compiler-derived from Table 2 dx,dy) by ~0.82 arcmin (~326 kpc, SE) and ~0.50 arcmin (~199 kpc, NW), significant at >4 sigma; within 500 kpc of gas peak: total 6.2(+1.2/-4.0)e14, gas 0.55+-0.06e14, stars 0.05+-0.01e14 Msun; LOS velocity difference 100+-80 km/s, merger speed ~2000 km/s (crude estimate).",
  "item3c_el_gordo": "Jee+2014 WL: M200c(NW)=1.38+-0.22e15, M200c(SE)=0.78+-0.20e15 h70^-1 Msun (ratio ~1.8), separation ~0.7 Mpc, combined M200a=3.13+-0.56e15; X-ray peak ~8 arcsec (~100 kpc) from SE mass peak (~2 sigma). Kim+2021 update: 9.9e14 / 6.5e14, total M200c=2.13e15 Msun. Menanteau+2012: sigma=1321+-106 km/s, TX=14.5 keV, Mgas=2.2e14, mass ratio ~2:1, LOS dv=586+-96 km/s.",
  "item3d_abell1689": "theta_E=47.0+-1.2 arcsec (zs=2); M2D(45\")=1.91+-0.27e14 Msun (Limousin+07); spherical M500=0.88+-0.13e15 and M200=1.15+-0.16e15 h^-1 Msun at r500=1.08, r200=1.60 h^-1 Mpc (Umetsu+15); concentration high: c200c~8-10 (lensing) vs predicted LCDM median log10 c200c = 0.58+-0.16 (i.e. ~3.8), only >~1-2 sigma tail after triaxiality. MOND with baryons alone fails (Nieuwenhuizen 2016/17; Hodson & Zhao 2017); MOND+~2 eV neutrinos can fit."
 },
